    {
      "parameters": {
        "schemaType": "manual",
        "inputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"suggested_title\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"A short, specific working title for this content\" },\n    \"core_message\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The single most important idea, in one or two sentences\" },\n    \"key_insights\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"description\": \"3 to 5 specific, non-obvious takeaways\" },\n    \"quotable_lines\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"description\": \"2 to 4 short verbatim lines worth quoting\" },\n    \"target_audience\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Who this content is for and what they care about\" },\n    \"hook_angles\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"description\": \"3 different angles that could open a post: contrarian, story, data, question\" },\n    \"tone\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The tone of the source, e.g. practical, provocative, educational\" }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"suggested_title\", \"core_message\", \"key_insights\", \"quotable_lines\", \"target_audience\", \"hook_angles\", \"tone\"]\n}"
      },
      "id": "bf46b57e-87d7-483c-826f-734cd642067a",
      "name": "Brief Parser",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        1552,
        1088
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a social media copywriter for YOUR BRAND NAME. Write platform-native drafts based on the content brief below. Every draft must stand on its own, stay faithful to the source, and never invent facts, numbers, or quotes that are not in the brief.\n\nBRAND VOICE:\n- Tone: professional and polished, but warm and approachable — never stiff or overly corporate.\n- Audience: everyday consumers, not industry insiders. Avoid jargon; explain benefits in plain, clear language.\n- Sentence style: confident, concise sentences. No hype, no excessive exclamation points, no clickbait phrasing.\n- Vocabulary: plain English. Contractions (e.g. \"you're,\" \"it's\") are fine — they keep things human without sacrificing polish.\n- Structure: lead with the value to the reader before any feature or technical detail.\n- Avoid: slang, emojis, ALL CAPS, aggressive sales language, or casual openers like \"hey guys.\"\n- Calls to action: clear and direct (e.g. \"Learn more,\" \"See how it works\") rather than urgency-driven or pushy.\n\nClear, confident, and practical. Short sentences. No hype words like \"game-changing\", \"unlock\", or \"revolutionary\". Speak to the reader as a smart peer, not a customer. Use plain English and concrete examples. British or American spelling: American.\n\nPLATFORM RULES\n- linkedin_post: 900 to 1,800 characters. Open with a one-line hook (never \"I'm excited to share\"). Short paragraphs with line breaks. End with a question or a clear call to action. No hashtags in the body; at most 3 on the final line.\n- x_thread: 4 to 7 tweets. Each tweet under 260 characters. Tweet 1 is the hook and must work on its own. Do NOT number the tweets; numbering is added later. Final tweet summarizes or points back to the source.\n- instagram_caption: 400 to 1,200 characters. First line is the hook (it shows before \"more\"). Conversational, line breaks between thoughts. No hashtags inside the caption.\n- hashtags: 8 to 15 specific, relevant Instagram hashtags as plain words without the # symbol.\n- newsletter_subject: under 50 characters, benefit or curiosity driven, no clickbait.\n- newsletter_blurb: 80 to 150 words teasing the content, with the link written as [LINK].\n- image_prompts: 2 to 3 prompts for an image generator describing a clean, on-brand visual. No text in the image, no logos, no people's faces.\n\nCONTENT BRIEF:\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.output, null, 2) }}\n\nSOURCE URL: {{ $('Normalize Content').first().json.sourceUrl || 'n/a' }}\nCAMPAIGN NOTES: {{ $('Normalize Content').first().json.notes || 'None' }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true
      },
      "id": "9d104e9c-f109-49e2-82fd-da79d2b0f5f7",
      "name": "Generate Platform Drafts",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.4,
      "position": [
        1888,
        832
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "schemaType": "manual",
        "inputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"linkedin_post\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"x_thread\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n    \"instagram_caption\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"hashtags\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n    \"newsletter_subject\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"newsletter_blurb\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"image_prompts\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"linkedin_post\", \"x_thread\", \"instagram_caption\", \"hashtags\", \"newsletter_subject\", \"newsletter_blurb\", \"image_prompts\"]\n}"
      },
      "id": "29beb8aa-d449-4d00-b65e-ed4155707e37",
      "name": "Drafts Parser",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        2048,
        1088
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Flattens the brief + drafts into one record whose keys match the Airtable field names exactly.\nconst brief = ($('Analyze Content').first().json.output) || {};\nconst drafts = ($input.first().json.output) || {};\nconst src = $('Normalize Content').first().json;\n\nconst tweets = Array.isArray(drafts.x_thread) ? drafts.x_thread : [];\nconst thread = tweets.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}/ ${String(t).trim()}`).join('\\n\\n');\n\n// Platform limit checks — surfaced in Slack and stored on the record.\nconst warnings = [];\nif ((drafts.linkedin_post || '').length > 3000) warnings.push('LinkedIn post is over 3,000 characters');\ntweets.forEach((t, i) => { if (String(t).length > 280) warnings.push(`Tweet ${i + 1} is over 280 characters`); });\nif ((drafts.instagram_caption || '').length > 2200) warnings.push('Instagram caption is over 2,200 characters');\n\nconst bullets = (arr) => (Array.isArray(arr) ? arr : []).map((x) => `• ${x}`).join('\\n');\nconst hashtags = (Array.isArray(drafts.hashtags) ? drafts.hashtags : [])\n  .map((h) => '#' + String(h).replace(/^#/, '').replace(/\\s+/g, ''))\n  .join(' ');\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    'Title': brief.suggested_title || src.title,\n    'Source URL': src.sourceUrl,\n    'Source Type': src.sourceType,\n    'Status': 'Draft',\n    'Core Message': brief.core_message || '',\n    'Key Insights': bullets(brief.key_insights),\n    'Target Audience': brief.target_audience || '',\n    'LinkedIn Post': drafts.linkedin_post || '',\n    'X Thread': thread,\n    'Instagram Caption': drafts.instagram_caption || '',\n    'Hashtags': hashtags,\n    'Newsletter Subject': drafts.newsletter_subject || '',\n    'Newsletter Blurb': drafts.newsletter_blurb || '',\n    'Image Prompts': bullets(drafts.image_prompts),\n    'Warnings': warnings.join('\\n'),\n  },\n}];"
      },
